\section{Overview}

The Zilog Z80 is the main processor in the Berzerk arcade machine, running at
2.5~MHz. This module implements the full Z80 instruction set following MAME's
emulator as the authoritative reference.

Key design decisions:
\begin{itemize}
\item Register pairs use [[PAIR16]] unions for dual 8/16-bit access
\item Flags stored as a composed byte with lookup tables for common patterns
\item All memory access goes through [[AddressSpace]] callbacks
\item The WZ (MEMPTR) internal register is tracked for undocumented flag behavior
\item Cycle counting uses per-instruction T-state costs
\end{itemize}

