\subsection{Register Pair Type}

The Z80's 8-bit registers are grouped into 16-bit pairs (BC, DE, HL, etc.).
MAME uses a union to allow access as either a 16-bit word or two 8-bit halves.
On little-endian machines (x86, ARM), the low byte comes first in memory.

<<pair16 type>>=
union PAIR16 {
    uint16_t w;
    struct {
        uint8_t l;  // low byte  (C, E, L, F)
        uint8_t h;  // high byte (B, D, H, A)
    } b;
};
@

\subsection{Flag Constants}

The Z80 flag register (F) encodes eight flags in a single byte. Bits 5 and 3
are the undocumented Y and X flags, which copy bits 5 and 3 of the result
for most ALU operations.

<<flag constants>>=
enum Z80Flag : uint8_t {
    CF = 0x01,  // Carry
    NF = 0x02,  // Subtract
    PF = 0x04,  // Parity/Overflow (shared bit)
    VF = 0x04,  // Overflow (alias for PF)
    XF = 0x08,  // Undocumented bit 3
    HF = 0x10,  // Half-carry
    YF = 0x20,  // Undocumented bit 5
    ZF = 0x40,  // Zero
    SF = 0x80,  // Sign
};
@

